# Patch1 edits line 55 of an existing alpha, while patch2 creates alpha from
# nothing with different content. Patch1's hunk describes a change against its
# own alpha, not the one patch2 writes, so the two never pair: the report must
# show patch2's creation, with its create-file and mode notes, and patch1's edit
# on patch1's side alone. tree-fill-fails covers the same pairing in tree mode;
# the operands are diffs of the wild and wildtip commits in the tree4 store.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 0
